---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
---
<PageLayout title="How TotalRecalls Works" description="Export AI chats to local Markdown and JSON in 4 steps." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "How It Works" }]}>
  <h1>How It Works</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls saves your AI conversations into a private folder on your computer — readable Markdown + JSON you keep forever. Four steps, start to finish.</p>

  <section class="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li><span class="step-icon">1</span><span><strong>Buy once</strong> — checkout via Lemon Squeezy. One-time $24 launch price, no subscription. You get a download link for the Windows app immediately.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">2</span><span><strong>Install</strong> — unzip and run TotalRecalls.exe. No installer, no background services, no account. Windows 10/11.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">3</span><span><strong>Pick a provider</strong> — ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (via Google Takeout), or Grok. You sign in locally, exactly like a browser.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-icon">4</span><span><strong>Export</strong> — conversations land in a Library folder on your PC as Markdown + JSON, organized per provider. Browse, search, or back them up anywhere.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Everything stays on your machine — a plain folder of files you own.</li>
      <li>Session tokens are used locally and never leave your PC.</li>
      <li>No cloud locker. No TotalRecalls account. Nothing to sign up for.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you get per provider</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ChatGPT</strong> — every conversation as Markdown + JSON, including images and metadata. See the <a href="/guides/export-chatgpt-conversations/">ChatGPT export guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Claude</strong> — Projects and long threads, kept as files. See the <a href="/guides/export-claude-chat-history/">Claude export guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Perplexity</strong> — research threads before you lose the tab trail. See the <a href="/guides/backup-perplexity-threads/">Perplexity export guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Gemini</strong> — uses your Google Takeout folder/JSON (the most reliable path). See the <a href="/guides/gemini-takeout-archive/">Gemini Takeout guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Grok</strong> — session scanning on grok.com. See the <a href="/guides/grok/">Grok export guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Will my provider block me?</strong> TotalRecalls works within each provider's own export/Takeout features — you must follow their terms.</li>
      <li><strong>Mac?</strong> Windows today (WebView2). Mac is planned if demand is real.</li>
      <li><strong>SmartScreen warning?</strong> Unsigned builds may show one — "More info → Run anyway". See the <a href="/guides/smartscreen/">SmartScreen help page</a>.</li>
      <li>More answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="footer-cta" style="background: var(--color-midnight); color: var(--color-surface); text-align: center;">
    <h2 style="color: var(--color-surface);">Ready to try it?</h2>
    <a href="/pricing/" class="buy-button buy-lg" data-tr-buy>Buy TotalRecalls — <span data-tr-price>$24</span></a>
    <p><a href="/download/" style="color: var(--color-surface);">Already purchased? Download ZIP</a></p>
  </section>

</PageLayout>
